      "id": "claim_b64411b9d78841f7965c19370e5445c8",
      "statement": "DevicePolicy.pin() performs exactly one `torch.cuda.set_device(local_rank)` side effect when CUDA is available and `local_rank < torch.cuda.device_count()`; an out-of-range LOCAL_RANK (>= device_count) skips `set_device` (the twin's tolerance semantics — never raise on a recoverable misconfig) while still returning `cuda:{local_rank}`, and when CUDA is unavailable pin() returns `torch.device(\"cpu\")` with zero side effects.",
