      "id": "claim_694dce7fcfa9496c87c043ae75ef8bf8",
      "statement": "DevicePolicy.warm_device(fallback) returns `cuda:{local_rank}` exactly when `fallback.type == \"cuda\"` and `torch.distributed.is_initialized()` (no `torch.cuda.is_available()` gate — a CUDA fallback under a live PG resolves even on a box without CUDA, byte-identical to the deleted `manifold.data.latent_pipeline.resolve_warm_device`); `torch.distributed` is imported lazily inside the method body so importing the `device_policy` module never touches the process group.",
